<p><strong>Power Issues</strong></p>
<p>The unit does a full boot instead of quick boot every time the accessori=
es is turned on. The Accessories G3 and Main battery power G2 are swapped a=
round so that G2 is coming on with ignition and G3 is always on.</p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G1=3D</s=
pan> 0VDC NEGATIVE</span><br><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D=
"color: #000000;">G2=3D 12VDC</span>&nbsp;<span style=3D"color: #ff2a00;">A=
CCESSORIES POWER (Swapped with G3)</span></span><br><span style=3D"color: #=
09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G3=3D 12VDC</span> <span style=3D"=
color: #ff2a00;">MAIN BATTERY (Swapped with G2</span></span></p>
<p>Correct Vehicle Voltage condition on these pins when ignition is <span s=
tyle=3D"text-decoration: underline;">ON</span>&nbsp;should be as follows:</=
p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G1=3D</s=
pan> 0VDC NEGATIVE</span><br><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D=
"color: #000000;">G2=3D</span> 12VDC MAIN BATTERY</span><br><span style=3D"=
color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G3=3D</span> 12VDC ACCESSO=
RIES POWER</span></p>
<p>Correct Vehicle Voltage condition on these pins when ignition is <span s=
tyle=3D"text-decoration: underline;">OFF</span>&nbsp;should be as follows:<=
/p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G1=3D</s=
pan> 0VDC NEGATIVE</span><br><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D=
"color: #000000;">G2=3D</span> 12VDC MAIN BATTERY</span><br><span style=3D"=
color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G3=3D</span> 0VDC ACCESSOR=
IES POWER</span></p>
<p><strong>The unit only comes on when the reset pin is pushed and held in =
and the optical light on the back comes&nbsp;on when the ignition is on.</s=
trong>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The<span style=3D"color: #000000;">&nbsp;accessories G3 is missing 12VDC=
.</span>&nbsp;You have the following condition which needs to be fixed.</p>
<p>Check for blown fuses, wire misalignment from factory pin to G plug or i=
f the G3 accessories is only supplied by canbus (not all cases), the canbus=
 could be faulty by not outputting 12VDC even if it has G2 main battery sup=
ply to it.</p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G1=3D</s=
pan> 0VDC NEGATIVE</span><br><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D=
"color: #000000;">G2=3D</span> 12VDC MAIN BATTERY</span><br><span style=3D"=
color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G3=3D</span> <span style=
=3D"color: #ff2a00;">0VDC ACCESSORIES POWER</span></span></p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #ff2a00;">Below is=
 an example of a symptom of 0VDC on G3 Accessories input</span></span></p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #ff2a00;"><img src=
=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/Screenshot_2023-=
07-22_at_6.50.41_am_480x480.png?v=3D1689979855" alt=3D""></span></span></p>
<p><strong>The fuse is blowing when the unit is connected, then the Negativ=
e G1 and Main Battery G2 are swapped</strong></p>
<p><strong>Please note: The unit has a 15A fuse, some vehicles accessories =
are lower than this and can blow. You may need to either upgrade the access=
ories fuse for your vehicle if it's safe to do so, or run a new accessories=
 line.</strong></p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G1=3D</s=
pan>&nbsp;<span style=3D"color: #ff2a00;">12VDC MAIN BATTERY</span></span><=
br><span style=3D"color: #ff2a00;"><span style=3D"color: #000000;">G2=3D&nb=
sp;</span>0VDC&nbsp;NEGATIVE</span><br><span style=3D"color: #09bc0c;"><spa=
n style=3D"color: #000000;">G3=3D</span> 12VDC ACCESSORIES POWER</span></p>
<p><strong><span>The unit turns off as expected by the battery is draining.=
</span></strong></p>
<p><span>Sometimes in some systems, the canbus (if installed) keeps somethi=
ng "awake" in the engine bay which drains the battery.</span></p>
<p><span>The solution is to disconnect the G2 mains battery supply to the c=
anbus, and power it by G3 accessories power only so that the canbus also tu=
rns off when the unit is off. <br>NOTE: If the G3 only comes from the canbu=
s only, then you will be required to run your own accessories power to the =
main power supply to the canbus instead.</span></p>
<p><span style=3D"color: #ff2a00;">IMPORTANT: some installations with this =
issue have been identified as having the reverse camera incorrectly install=
ed to the main battery G2 instead of the accessories. This will cause the c=
amera to stay on all the time and drain the battery.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><strong>When I crank the key from accessory to ignition, the HU screen g=
oes black for 1-2 seconds and then comes back. Is this normal?</strong></p>
<div><span color=3D"#ff4013" style=3D"color: #000000;">This can happen if t=
he&nbsp;vehicle is&nbsp;be cutting the accessories off when switching betwe=
en accessories to ignition</span></div>
<div><span color=3D"#ff4013" style=3D"color: #000000;">You can go into gene=
ral settings and increasing the =E2=80=9Cdelay off=E2=80=9D setting&nbsp;</=
span></div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>My unit is not fast booting from start</span></strong></p>
<p><span>Check in your Factory settings if you have Sleep Mode selected ON<=
/span></p>
<p><span>In general settings, set sleep delay to 3 seconds.</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>My USB port / ports are&nbsp;not working.</span></strong><=
/p>
<ol>
<li>Check the connection for Port D (USB1) and E (USB2/3) and make sure the=
y are pushed all the way in and seated correctly.</li>
<li>Check the USB1 &amp; USB2/3 cables for any damaged cables or loose wire=
s.</li>
<li>Check that the <span>socket D and E</span> pins are not bent or damaged=
</li>
<li>Measure the voltage on pins 1 to 3 on socket D and E for 5VDC</li>
<li>If you measure 5VDC then it is fine</li>
<li>If no voltage if found on these pins, try to perform a factory reset Se=
ttings - User - Backup/reset - 168 - clear all data</li>
<li>Unplug the canbus wait 5 minutes and plug it back in again.</li>
<li>If still no success, send back for warranty repair</li>
</ol>
<p>NOTE: If not using the supplied USB cables direct to the unit and instea=
d using retention to the vehicles original USB port, this might not be comp=
atible.</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/USB_p=
ort_pins_600x600.jpg?v=3D1674708064" alt=3D""></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>Whenever&nbsp;I start the unit the WIFI has to be turned o=
n again. How do&nbsp;I keep the units WIFI on?</span></strong></p>
<p>Swipe the screen down to reveal the Wifi icon, Press and hold it to open=
 the WIFI options and do the follow the below steps.</p>
<p>1) Enter Wifi preferences&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/93=
32/files/wifi_1_600x600.png?v=3D1673319944" alt=3D""></span></strong></p>
<p>2) Turn on WIFI Automatically</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/wifi_=
2_600x600.png?v=3D1673320057" alt=3D""></p>
<p><strong>My GPS tracking of position is not as smooth/accurate as when I =
use Android Auto/Apple Carplay</strong></p>
<p><span>Check that your GPS antenna connection is secured. This is the mos=
t common cause.</span></p>
<p><span>You can check the GPS signal strength in the Settings --&gt; Devic=
e --&gt; GPS section</span><strong><span><br><br>I have an issue where I wi=
ll be playing radio and it automatically mutes itself when the vehicle stop=
/start is triggered.</span></strong></p>
<p>Go to settings - Factory Settings - 168 - Start/Stop Enable</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>When flicking my interior lights on and off the unit cycles app =
modes, also it does not always start when turning the car on till&nbsp;I do=
 a reset</strong></p>
<p>Perform a factory reset - settings --&gt; user --&gt; Backup/reset &nbsp=
;- 168 --&gt; Clear all data. This rare occurrence has been reported to be =
resolved with this method.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>I have OEM amplifier but its not turning on.</span></stron=
g></p>
<p><span>If the supplied harness supports OEM amplifier, it should have a B=
LUE AMP wire. Connect this to either G3 Accessories, or to Blue AMP-C that =
is on the supplied CC3 AUX harness that has the sim card reader on it.</spa=
n></p>
<p><img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/fi=
les/amp_wire_480x480.jpg?v=3D1720689039"></p>
<p><strong><span>My screen is not dimming and&nbsp;the side capacitive butt=
ons are not illuminating when&nbsp;I turn the head lights on.<br></span></s=
trong></p>
<p><span>Settings --&gt; General --&gt; Disable Backlight Control</span></p=
>
<p><strong><span><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/93=
32/files/Screen_Shot_2022-11-07_at_12.25.20_am_600x600.png?v=3D1667752062" =
alt=3D""></span></strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>My screen is flickering dark and bright.</strong></p>
<p>If you have non-canbus safe LED that has replaced your glove box light a=
nd there is no glove box switch, change the LED back to&nbsp;the normal&nbs=
p;<span>incandescent globe.</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>My screen dim for head lights is in manual mode and no timer is =
active. My screen does not DIM to the settings I put when&nbsp;I turn my he=
ad lights on.</strong></p>
<p>If your instrument panel illumination also controls the dashboard lights=
 illumination, then please check that your instrument panel illumination di=
al is turned up above its lowest level.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>How do&nbsp;I set my day time and night time screen bright=
ness levels?</span></strong></p>
<p>Settings --&gt; Device --&gt; Display --&gt; Brightness Level</p>
<p><strong><span><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/93=
32/files/Screen_Shot_2022-11-07_at_12.32.20_am_600x600.png?v=3D1667752361" =
alt=3D""></span></strong></p>
<p><strong><span><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/93=
32/files/Screen_Shot_2022-11-07_at_12.34.11_am_600x600.png?v=3D1667752468" =
alt=3D""></span></strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>How do&nbsp;I enable/turn off A/C display?</span></strong>=
</p>
<p><span>If your OEM head unit supports this function it should carry over =
most times to the unit. To turn on/off this setting</span></p>
<p><span>Settings --&gt; Factory --&gt; 168 --&gt; Car Agreement --&gt; A/C=
 Information ON/OFF</span></p>
<p><span><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files=
/a_c_display_600x600.jpg?v=3D1666801309" alt=3D""></span></p>
<p><strong><span>My default volume is too loud/quiet, how do&nbsp;I adjust =
it?</span></strong></p>
<p><span>Go to settings --&gt; General --&gt; Enable Default Volume Switch =
--&gt; Open Default boot volume option and set to your desired level</span>=
</p>
<p><span><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files=
/Screen_Shot_2022-10-25_at_10.32.47_pm_600x600.png?v=3D1666708486" alt=3D""=
></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>My boot screen logo option is missing or not opening in fa=
ctory settings.</span></strong></p>
<p><span>(i) If its not opening, install this fix from (</span><a href=3D"h=
ttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1pQrVzqtjPxpjqM0nocdiJZw-VNmQXyZS/view?usp=
=3Dsharing" target=3D"_blank" aria-describedby=3D"a11y-new-window-external-=
message" rel=3D"null noopener">here</a><span>)</span></p>
<p>(ii) If it is missing, Install the latest firmware for your head unit fr=
om (<a href=3D"https://teyes.com.au/pages/tech-portal" target=3D"_blank" ar=
ia-describedby=3D"a11y-new-window-external-message" rel=3D"null noopener">h=
ere</a>). Once installed and showing, if its not opening, install this fix =
from (<a href=3D"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pQrVzqtjPxpjqM0nocdiJZw-V=
NmQXyZS/view?usp=3Dsharing" target=3D"_blank" aria-describedby=3D"a11y-new-=
window-external-message" rel=3D"null noopener">here</a>) as above (i)</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/Scree=
n_Shot_2022-10-25_at_7.35.45_pm_600x600.png?v=3D1666697774" alt=3D""></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>My steering controls volume and seek buttons are reversed.&nbsp;=
</strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span>Go to Settings --&gt; Factory --&gt; 168 --&gt; Original Car Agree=
ment --&gt; Reversal Previous and Next and also&nbsp;Reversal Volume</span>=
</p>
<p><span><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files=
/reversal_buttons_600x600.png?v=3D1672677704" alt=3D""></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>My OEM unit used to display my A/C, how can&nbsp;I do it?</stron=
g></p>
<p>Depending on your vehicle, you must have the correct canbus settings ent=
ered. Also you should check the following below. If your OEM head unit did =
not show such data, or it is a trim level not supported by our package, it =
will not be carried over.</p>
<p>Go to Settings --&gt; Factory --&gt; 168 --&gt; Original Car Agreement -=
-&gt; A/C information ON/OFF --&gt; Toggle to the Right</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/Scree=
n_Shot_2022-10-07_at_11.40.26_pm_600x600.png?v=3D1665157581" alt=3D""></p>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>My unit is not sleeping, but performing a full boot on start</st=
rong></p>
<p>Go to Settings --&gt; Factory&nbsp;--&gt; 168 --&gt;&nbsp;if Sleep mode =
setting is off (to the left) toggle it on (to the right), If it is already =
ON (to the right) toggle it OFF and ON again.</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/Untit=
led-75_copy_600x600.jpg?v=3D1664977441" alt=3D""></p>
<p><strong>When&nbsp;I try to open my app draw it is blank</strong></p>
<p>Do a factory reset, Settings --&gt; User --&gt; Backup/Reset --&gt; 168 =
--&gt; Clear All Data</p>
<p>You will need to change your language back <a href=3D"https://teyes.com.=
au/blogs/news/how-to-change-languages?_pos=3D1&amp;_sid=3Db08c13090&amp;_ss=
=3Dr" target=3D"_blank" aria-describedby=3D"a11y-new-window-external-messag=
e" rel=3D"null noopener">(guide is here)</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>When I do a full boot, my vehicle brand logo I selected isn't sh=
owing.</strong></p>
<p>Do a factory reset, Settings --&gt; User --&gt; Backup/Reset --&gt; 168 =
--&gt; Clear All Data</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span>You will need to change your language back </span><a href=3D"https=
://teyes.com.au/blogs/news/how-to-change-languages?_pos=3D1&amp;_sid=3Db08c=
13090&amp;_ss=3Dr" target=3D"_blank" aria-describedby=3D"a11y-new-window-ex=
ternal-message" rel=3D"null noopener">(guide is here)</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>My "Themes" keeps reseting to another theme.</strong></p>
<p>If you are running the latest firmware and having this issue, please do =
the following:</p>
<p>Go to Settings --&gt; Device --&gt; Apps --&gt; Health Monitoring Servic=
e --&gt; Disable</p>
<p>This service is mainly for mobile devices and not required.</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>This keeps popping up on my screen when changing launchers.</str=
ong></p>
<p>Update to the latest firmware (<a href=3D"https://teyes.com.au/pages/tec=
h-portal" target=3D"_blank" aria-describedby=3D"a11y-new-window-external-me=
ssage" rel=3D"null noopener">here</a>)</p>
<p>Once updated, reconnect the unit to the internet and reboot is required.=
<br><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/Scre=
en_Shot_2022-10-10_at_12.57.32_am_600x600.png?v=3D1665334668" alt=3D""></p>
<p><strong>How do&nbsp;I change my time settings to 24hr?</strong></p>
<p>Go to Settings --&gt; System --&gt; Date and Time --&gt; Use 24-hour for=
mat</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/files/Scree=
n_Shot_2022-11-03_at_12.16.08_pm_600x600.png?v=3D1667448988" alt=3D""></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>My GPS stopped working, how can&nbsp;I fix it?</strong></p>
<p>1) Check that the SMA connection at the rear of the head unit is not loo=
se</p>
<p>2) Check for any cabling damage</p>
<p>3) Swipe the screen down and select "Reboot"</p>
<p>4) If that does not work, perform a factory reset</p>
<p>Settings --&gt; User --&gt; Backup/Reset --&gt; 168 --&gt; Clear All Dat=
a</p>
<p>5) If each of those steps do not resolve the problem, replace the GPS do=
ngle</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>I sound very quiet with the internal mic, but also when&nbsp;I d=
isable the internal mic and use the external microphone.</strong></p>
<p>A reported working solution is a factory reset</p>
<p>Settings --&gt; User --&gt; Backup/Reset --&gt; 168 --&gt; Clear All Dat=
a</p>
<p><strong>There is a "str_release_space_fail" prompt coming up on the bott=
om of the screen. What does this mean?</strong></p>
<p>This is for 360 systems. It means that the 360 recording video drive is =
full. You need to format it.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>When ever I start my car the unit starts. When I turn on the hea=
d lights of my car the power to the head unit goes out. When I turn off the=
 head light the power comes back to the head unit.</strong></p>
<p>We found that this issue was due to the connections not being connected =
properly<br><br></p>
<p><strong>TEYES DVR stops recording,&nbsp;whenever the DVR app is displaye=
d at first it begins to record and will do so for a few minutes then stops.=
 If I display any other app momentarily, it will start recording again once=
 it is displayed, but only for about the same duration.</strong></p>
<p>This was resolved by changing to another microSD card. 6GB is also the r=
ecommended maximum storage size.</p>
<p style=3D"font-weight: 400;"><strong><span>Although android auto WIRELESS=
 is not officially supported on the CC3. Some phones are connecting but som=
e have connection issues which are resolved with the below steps.</span></s=
trong></p>
<ol style=3D"font-weight: 400;">
<li><em><span>Clear the Google Services cache - Text tutorial Open Settings=
-&gt;Apps &amp; notifications-&gt;Google Play services-&gt;Storage &amp; Ca=
che-&gt;Clear Storage</span></em></li>
<li><em><span>Clear Android Auto cache - Text tutorial Open Phone Settings-=
&gt;Apps &amp; Notifications-&gt;Android Auto-&gt;Storage &amp; Cache-&gt;C=
lear Storage</span></em></li>
<li><em><span>Upgrade Android Auto and Google Map in Google Store on your p=
hone</span></em></li>
<li><em><span>Restart the phone, ignore all Bluetooth in your phone (CK: th=
is means delete all Bluetooth connections.</span></em></li>
<li><em><span>First use the data cable to connect the phone and the box int=
o the wired Android Auto, connect successfully and then disconnect the data=
 cable to reconnect the wireless Android Auto (CK: and also start the Autok=
it app)</span></em></li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"font-weight: 400;">&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Apple Music app is not working.</strong></p>
<p>Uninstall and re-install again. The music will need to be re-downloaded<=
/p>
<p><br><img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/933=
2/files/imagedd0_600x600.jpg?v=3D1705688189"></p>
