such as Gesture and UI Server apps. You do not have to worry about these an=
d you cannot remove them.</strong></p>
<p><img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0529/8837/9332/fi=
les/Screenshot_2024-02-13_at_5.11.13_pm_600x600.png?v=3D1707815501"></p>
<p><strong>Samsung Work Profile - Teams issue</strong></p>
<p><strong></strong><span>My samsung has a work profile and inside that pro=
file is Teams. When I receive a call I need to receive the call on my phone=
, not the head unit. It seams as though when the teams call is ended, the u=
nit holds onto the phone Bluetooth connection and you cannot get audio thro=
ugh stereo at all. </span></p>
<div dir=3D"auto">The only way to unhook it from the connection is to call =
voicemail, then all is ok. Rebooting or restarting the car doesn't make a d=
ifference, calling voicemail resets the unit to knowing it's a phone call a=
nd when you hang-up from voicemail it naturally switches back to the stereo=
.&nbsp;</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><strong>When I'm driving spontaneously the app I am curre=
ntly using swaps to the standard radio app and starts playing radio. I then=
 need to navigate back to the app I was using. Any way to prevent this from=
 happening?</strong></div>
<div dir=3D"auto">
<strong></strong><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">This&nbsp;issue is&nbsp;caused from&nbsp;connecting the p=
hone via usb cable and having&nbsp;wireless Android Auto turned on at the s=
ame time.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><strong>After updating the firmware, the voice commands i=
n google maps app is only supported in English.</strong></div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Perform a factory reset and this should resolve the issue=
.</div>
